## std::proof — proof-construction helpers for agent verification workflows.
##
## `assert` is a tool declaration so runtimes can route failures to a
## structured exception channel. `assume_for_proof` is a pure helper that
## introduces a hypothesis into the current reasoning context.

## Assert that `cond` is true, throwing if it is not.
## Use in verification workflows where a violated invariant must halt execution.
tool assert(cond: Bool, msg: Str) -> Unit !{Throw}

## Introduce a boolean hypothesis for proof purposes (pure, no runtime effect).
## Returns unit; the value of `p` is the interesting part.
fn assume_for_proof(p: Bool) -> Unit effects {} {
  ()
}

## Logical negation of a boolean (explicit named helper for readability).
fn proof_not(p: Bool) -> Bool effects {} {
  !p
}

## True iff both `a` and `b` hold.
fn proof_and(a: Bool, b: Bool) -> Bool effects {} {
  a && b
}

## True iff at least one of `a` or `b` holds.
fn proof_or(a: Bool, b: Bool) -> Bool effects {} {
  a || b
}
